  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Summer 2005 held nine tournaments in seven cities from 10 July to 14 August 2005, some of them at Pokémon Festa 2005, with places drawn by lottery among players who applied in advance. Everyone in the qualifying round got Hiromichi Sugiyama's cosmos holofoil Rayquaza and finalists a holo React Energy. Every tournament had two third places, so the Victory Orb, redrawn that year with Mew, went to the top four of each division: 108 copies. The winners went on to the Champion's League in Tokyo that September.",
